    "description": "•\tDesigned and developed a large Java enterprise application (20,000+ source files) that covers a wide array of functionality including Order Entry, Warehouse Management, Print On Demand, Shipping, Outbound/Inbound Response Management, Lead Management, Localization, Reporting, and System Administration.  The application serves 50+ clients in various industries, such as bank, financial, and healthcare.\n•\tThe application is in Service-oriented and MVC Architecture which utilizes AngularJS and JSP as the front end, Servlets and Business Objects as the middle tier, Hibernate as the ORM, SQL Server as database, and Midas as an external warehouse.\n•\tSome sample functionality in this diverse application includes the ability to place personalized orders, create custom books that generate PDFs on the fly, complete phone agent support, complex security administration, advanced item maintenance, custom reporting and graphing, and much more. \n•\tSolely responsible for the Order Processing module, which is the core of the Order Entry feature. It handles tens of thousands of orders across 50+ accounts daily.  For every order, it manages Kits, Replacements, Supplements, Alternative items, and Lot Control items back-and-forth between the application and warehouse.\n•\tWorked on Hadoop (Splice Machine) conversion from an Oracle database.\n•\tDeveloped Single sign-on (SOAP and SAML depending on client needs) for many external clients.\n•\tDeveloped XML Web Services (RESTful and SOAP) to expose functionality for both internal and external clients.\n•\tDeveloped numerous import and export routines to integrate with 3rd party vendors and clients on an ongoing basis.\n•\tDeveloped numerous Transact-SQL Stored Procedures to optimize database access in various databases.  \n•\tDeveloped numerous Informix Stored Procedures to manipulate data in the Midas warehouse.\n•\tTechnical lead for projects involving 4+ engineers.\n",
